      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8x-48y+80z &=104 \\\\ x-6y+10z &=13 \\\\ -2x+12y-20z &=-26\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & -48 & 80 & 104 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 10 & 13 \\\\ -2 & 12 & -20 & -26\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_2\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -6 & 10 & 13 \\\\ 8 & -48 & 80 & 104 \\\\ -2 & 12 & -20 & -26\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-8)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -6 & 10 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 12 & -20 & -26\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(2)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -6 & 10 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-6y+10z &=13 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system.\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z$. That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=13+6y-10z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z\\end{aligned}\\right.,\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}13+6y-10z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\n",
